    Add in-band line control (-E), resident mode (-L/-U), CI emulator tests
    
    In-band line control (-E): QEMU never drops DCD when the socket to the BBS
    closes, so carrier and DTR travel in the byte stream using DOSBox-X's
    nullmodem framing (FF FF literal, FF nn line state). The BBS sends FF 00
    before closing on hangup; FOSSIL 06h sends FF 01/FF 03 to the BBS.
    
    Resident mode: -L loads WWIVFOSS as a TSR, -U unloads it through a private
    INT 14h API (AH=7Eh, BX='WF'). Unload refuses if INT 14h or the UART IRQ
    was hooked after us, and leaves the memory allocated if any other vector
    still points into it.
    
    Also:
    - uart: interrupt-driven TX ring; block writes no longer come up short
      on emulators that model serial timing (DOSBox-X)
    - runner: spawn .EXE/.COM doors directly so the exit code comes back
    - uart: wait two ticks after draining on close; DOSBox-X drops up to
      256 bytes of buffered output when it exits
    - FOSTEST: H lowers DTR (exit 3); Q/H are uppercase only
    - tests: echo/hangup/dtr scenarios x runner/resident, QEMU with -E and
      DOSBox-X raw; harness in Python; all 10 pass
    - CI: runs the full emulator matrix; actions moved off Node 20

