    Initial WWIVFOSS: FOSSIL runner for DOS doors
    
    WWIVFOSS installs a FOSSIL revision 5 INT 14h handler, runs a door, and
    removes itself when the door exits. Transports are pluggable; this commit
    implements the uart transport for emulators (QEMU, DOSBox-X) whose COM
    port is connected to a TCP socket the BBS listens on.
    
    - dos/: runner, FOSSIL dispatcher (00h-1Bh), signature entry stub, 16550
      driver with interrupt-driven 2 KB rx/tx rings, idle timeslice release
    - tools/fostest: FOSSIL exerciser door used by the tests
    - scripts/: Open Watcom + FreeDOS dev environment, build, end-to-end
      tests under QEMU and DOSBox-X with a Python BBS harness, FreeDOS shell
    - docs/design.md: architecture, interrupt-safety rules, open questions
    - vdd (NTVDM) and OS/2 pipe transports are placeholders
    
    Tests: qemu/echo, dosbox/echo and dosbox/hangup pass. qemu/hangup fails
    because QEMU doesn't drop DCD when the socket closes; that needs the
    planned in-band control mode.
